coding=\"async\" src=\"..\/wp-content\/uploads\/2016\/02\/star2.gif\" class=\"rstars\" \/><img decoding=\"async\" src=\"..\/wp-content\/uploads\/2016\/02\/star2.gif\" class=\"rstars\" \/><br \/>\nQuestion:<br \/>\nCan a server stand between side lines and serve in a double game?<\/p>\n<p>Answer:<br \/>\nHi Sudhir, unfortunately no, a server must stand inside \u2026<\/p>\n<\/div>\n<div class=\"othervisitors\">\n<p><a href=\"if-both-partners-serve-while-standing-in-the-same-box-is-that-a-foul.html\"><b>If both partners serve while standing in the same box, is that a foul?<\/b><\/a>\u00a0<br \/>\n<b>Question:<\/b> Is it a fault if both partners are in the same box while serving?<\/p>\n<p><b>Answer:<\/b><br \/>\nHi Raj, thanks for asking us a question.<\/p>\n<p>In doubles, \u2026<\/p>\n<\/div>\n<div class=\"othervisitors\">\n<p><a href=\"service-rules-must-players-stand-still-when-delivering-or-receiving-a-serve.html\"><b>Service Rules: Must Players Stand Still When Delivering or Receiving a Serve?<\/b><\/a>\u00a0<br \/>\nQuestion:<br \/>\nCould you please answer this question? In doubles, when the player is ready to serve and the receiver is ready must the other players be still \u2026<\/p>\n<\/div>\n<div class=\"othervisitors\">\n<p><a href=\"badminton-serving-rules.html\"><b>Badminton serving rules<\/b><\/a>\u00a0<br \/>\nQuestion: Player A serves to player B who was running to return the shot. Player B misses the shot but the shuttle hits his body while he was outside \u2026<\/p>\n<\/div>\n<div class=\"othervisitors\">\n<p><a href=\"serving-rules-must-both-feet-be-stationary-during-a-serve.html\"><b>Serving rules: Must both feet be stationary during a serve? <\/b><\/a>\u00a0<br \/>\nQuestion: Greetings from Kelowna, B.C Canada. Must the server&#8217;s feet be still when he serves? In other words, can he walk and serve at the same time? \u2026<\/p>\n<\/div>\n<div class=\"othervisitors\">\n<p><a href=\"what-are-the-rules-of-serving-in-a-singles-game.html\"><b>What are the rules of serving in a singles game?<\/b><\/a>\u00a0<br \/>\nQuestion: What are the rules to serve in single game? (I don&#8217;t know the proper rules that&#8217;s why I am asking you)<\/p>\n<p>Answer:<\/p>\n<p>Hi Prateeksha, thank \u2026<\/p>\n<\/div>\n<div class=\"othervisitors\">\n<p><a href=\"winning-points-and-the-rules-of-service.html\"><b>Winning points and the rules of service<\/b><\/a>\u00a0<br \/>\nQuestion: Can receiver get a point if it is the opponents serve and he makes the fault?<\/p>\n<p>Answer:<br \/>\nHi Chinar, thank you for your question.<\/p>\n<p>Yes, \u2026<\/p>\n<\/div>\n<div class=\"othervisitors\">\n<p><a href=\"in-badminton-the-server-can-serve-anywhere-from-his-service-court-is-possible.html\"><b>In badminton the server can serve anywhere from his service court is possible?<\/b><\/a>\u00a0<br \/>\nQuestion:<br \/>\nIn badmintion the server can serve anywhere from his service court is possible?<\/p>\n<p>Answer:<br \/>\nHi Bijo (nice name by the way), thanks for the \u2026<\/p>\n<\/div>\n<div class=\"othervisitors\">\n<p><a href=\"service-rules-in-detail.html\"><b>Service Rules in detail<\/b><\/a>\u00a0<br \/>\nQuestions:<br \/>\nI&#8217;ve seen a few questions on service rules but I&#8217;m just still confused so I&#8217;m making this post.<\/p>\n<p>1. Where is the highest level the shuttlecock \u2026<\/p>\n<\/div>\n<div class=\"othervisitors\">\n<p><a href=\"must-the-racket-head-be-fully-or-partially-below-the-servers-waist-during-service.html\"><b>Must the racket head be fully or partially below the server&#8217;s waist during service?<\/b><\/a>\u00a0<br \/>\nQuestion: Must the racket head be fully or partially below the server&#8217;s waist during service?<\/p>\n<p>I only see a rule stating that the birdie must be under \u2026<\/p>\n<\/div>\n<div class=\"othervisitors\">\n<p><a href=\"serving-rule-waist-height.html\"><b>Serving Rule (waist height)<\/b><\/a>\u00a0<br \/>\nQuestion: I am used to giving service while placing shuttle on